From: McKernel Rust migration <mckernel@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] rust: expose existing x86 APIC driver declarations

Allow the native SMP adapter to check the active driver's physical-destination
contract before using Linux's already exported APIC mask static call. This adds
only the existing architecture header to bindgen's input; no C function body or
export changes.

--- a/rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h
+++ b/rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@
  * Sorted alphabetically.
  */
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_X86_64
+#include <asm/apic.h>
+#endif
+
 #include <kunit/test.h>
 #include <linux/blk-mq.h>
 #include <linux/blk_types.h>
